  "title": "Firebreak Crews and Shared Rescue Routes",
  "rules": [
    "Crew cannot enter walls, burning cells or smoke level three. Simultaneous occupancy conflicts block movement; even a blocked direction updates facing.",
    "Spray spends one carried water unit on the facing cell. All sprays resolve before clear actions; clearing permanently removes unburning fuel.",
    "Every third live step, burning cells can ignite orthogonal fuel-bearing neighbors. Current fire consumes one fuel before the next flame grid is stored.",
    "A crew may carry one survivor. Move the survivor into x <= 1 and y <= 1 to rescue. Injured disabled carriers release their survivor.",
    "A finite tank refills one unit per action. Facing-adjacent crews can transfer a unit; cyclic role priority resolves all contested custody and supply actions.",
    "Fire and level-three smoke cause persistent health loss. Shared and priority rewards record rescues and losses; exhausted crews retain a legal wait."
  ],
